# Railway Environment Variables Template for Student Clearance System
# Copy these to your Railway service's Variables tab

# ===== DATABASE CONFIGURATION =====
# Option 1: Use Railway PostgreSQL (automatic when you link PostgreSQL)
# The following variables are automatically set by Railway:
# PGHOST=postgres.railway.internal
# PGPORT=5432
# PGDATABASE=railway
# PGUSER=postgres
# PGPASSWORD=<your-railway-password>

# Option 2: Manual connection string (if using external database)
# Uncomment and fill this if NOT using Railway PostgreSQL:
# ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection=postgresql://username:password@hostname:5432/database_name

# ===== INITIAL ADMIN ACCOUNT =====
# REQUIRED: Admin password for first login
InitialAdmin__Password=SecureAdminPass123!

# OPTIONAL: Admin email (defaults to admin@university.edu)
# InitialAdmin__Email=admin@university.edu

# ===== APPLICATION SETTINGS =====
# These are already configured in appsettings.json but can be overridden here if needed:
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production
# AllowedHosts=*

# ===== INSTRUCTIONS =====
# 1. If using Railway PostgreSQL:
#    - Go to Railway dashboard
#    - Click "+ Add" and select PostgreSQL
#    - Wait for database to be provisioned
#    - The PGHOST, PGPORT, PGDATABASE, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD will be automatically available
#    - Set InitialAdmin__Password below
#    - Redeploy

# 2. If using external PostgreSQL:
#    - Uncomment the ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection line
#    - Fill in your database credentials
#    - Set InitialAdmin__Password below
#    - Redeploy

# 3. After deployment:
#    - Access the application at your Railway service URL
#    - Login with admin@university.edu and the password from InitialAdmin__Password
